WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.219
Some people worry that big tech
companies are seducing you into spending

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:15.669
more time online, all so they can monetize
your data. Is this true? Yes, but not in a

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:20.140
bad way! Big tech companies do try to get
you to consume more of their services,

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.640
just like Starbucks and the New York
Times do. This is normal. Is consuming

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.360
more tech bad for you?
Studies show that spending more time on

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.860
Facebook is associated with greater
obesity, less well being, and less real

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:37.329
time with friends. But this is also true
for television. And if you interact with

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:40.660
your friends on Facebook, your sense of
well-being is actually higher, and you

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:45.310
feel more socially connected. But don't
the tech companies gather lots of data

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.079
on you that they use to their advantage?
Absolutely, but this is also normal.

00:00:50.079 --> 00:00:54.820
President Obama made social media micro-targeting of voters famous. Tech

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:59.829
companies just need to be transparent
about their real business. Big tech is

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:04.930
doing what others have done before, only
in a bigger way, and big tech's successors

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.620
will do it even bigger.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:10.980
What do you think?
Does big tech know too much about you?

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:15.880
Let us know your comments. Also, let us
know what other topics you'd like our

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:21.460
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.260
research and videos from AEI.

